The Linux filesystem wrapper's only skip condition is non-Linux. Its source
acceptance requires all four generated cases, private mount/root and Landlock
checks, same-UID host/proc-root access denial, read-only canary checks, bounded
tmpfs exhaustion, permanent privilege drop, inherited-authority closure,
three WorkerRun invocations/six ranks, four global/eight rank optimizer steps,
and exact cleanup of four cgroups/mountpoints/sentinel processes. The passing
Linux source run establishes this generated acceptance under that test contract.

## Corrections retained in history

The original filesystem commit `741639cc3eac16a4fa844c886350159f55e1e56a` failed
before normal-case mount setup completed. Its successor
`5ab44f96b677cc23f70c6f34eff79f7a55716eac` corrected namespace-affinity of pinned
bind sources and advanced to a WorkerRun failure. Both failed runs remain
preserved, with confirmed owned cleanup; neither was rerun unchanged or deleted.

The accepted successor adds a verified-private-root READ_DIR-only opt-in for
the unchanged loader's ancestor walk, plus allowlisted WorkerRun failure
projection. It does not grant root file-content read/write/execute permission.
The failure report from the prior run did not prove its exact inner failure;
the source-AST regression independently established the directory-walk contract
conflict, and the new remote result establishes end-to-end generated acceptance.

Local verification was 939 stdlib-only tests, no failures/errors/skips,
`ML_MODULES_LOADED=False`, exact Ruff and Linux-file AST checks. No Linux
fixture/wrapper or ML runtime was imported or executed on the Mac. The older
netns, cgroup and WorkerRun fixtures remain byte-for-byte bound and unchanged.
Tracked code is clean after publication; unrelated untracked files are excluded.

## Roadmap handoff

The generated filesystem isolation/compatibility substep is now accepted.
Gate 5 as a whole remains partial. Next source/design work is the trusted
runtime/filesystem handoff and real-host admission binding, including residual
pathname-UNIX IPC authority within exposed trusted trees. Complete hostile
process containment, runtime origin and real-host admission are not proved here.

Real-size import/relocation and actual H100 validation remain separate later
work. No GPU instance, S3 object, pretrained model, real dataset, inference,
training, registry, promotion or dataset seal was touched. Real-SFT admission
and production eligibility remain false. No additional CI run was started
after the accepted result.
